.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="On the Rosenbrock function from (-1.2, 1.0), BFGS builds an inverse-Hessian approximation from gradients alone. It needs only a few dozen iterations, as few as Newton&#x27;s method with the exact Hessian at every step, while gradient descent needs thousands. Near the minimum its convergence is superlinear: the ratio of successive errors tends to zero.">

